  "narrative": "Starting from a baseline around historical annual tolls, the observed pace in early 2026 strongly suggests a real risk of reaching 1,000 deaths in the Mediterranean by May. While there are countervailing factors like potential SAR improvements, the balance of evidence points toward a high probability of crossing the threshold, with some uncertainty due to reporting lags and environmental conditions.",
  "justification": {
    "anchor": {
      "probability": 0.60,
      "basis": "reference class anchored on long-run central Mediterranean fatalities (roughly 1.8k–2.5k annually); early 2026 data (606 by February) used as the starting point, representing a meaningful uplift from the baseline."
